  "match": true,
  "comparison": "Exact async attempt/update/release counts and deterministic backoff delays for simulated Windows permission errors, persistent/non-Windows errors, ordinary contention, mixed counters and cancellation. Real separate processes verify writes wait for another holder and preserve both provider entries.",
  "limitations": "Windows platform/error inputs are injected like Pi source tests; a real Windows delete-pending filesystem is unavailable. Pi uses proper-lockfile directories; PiSharp uses persistent private native FileShare.None leases and separate process gates. Both async policy contracts match; PiSharp exposes no synchronous auth-storage API. Cross-language simultaneous locking of the same auth file, lease timeout wording and wider auth refresh/reload semantics remain open.",
  "characterization": {
    "log": "artifacts/parity/current-pi-deltas-2026-10-13/auth-lock-fail-first.log",
    "sha256": "b153f1f9654a012fd0ee31899c6729c1c29b1589b86cd9dbae1bd6a50b663f4d",
    "failed": 2,
    "passed": 0,
    "skipped": 0,
    "finding": "Two deterministic mismatches: 20 independent concurrent storage writes retained one provider entry, and storage writes ignored a held native credential-file lease."
  },
  "sourceVerification": {
    "command": "npx --cache /tmp/pisharp-npm-cache vitest run packages/coding-agent/test/auth-storage.test.ts --reporter=json --outputFile=/tmp/pisharp-current-auth-lock-source-tests.json",
    "passed": 30,
    "failed": 0,
    "skipped": 0
  },
  "implementation": "AuthStorage uses a process gate shared by normalized credential-file path and a persistent private .pisharp.lock FileShare.None lease. Mutations hold the native lease until the atomic replacement is complete. Read/list operations retain read-only access and use a shared process gate plus FileShare.Delete snapshots of atomically replaced credential files; lookups do not create absent agent directories. OAuth refresh locks reuse the acquisition owner while retaining their existing two-minute contention budget. Windows access-denied/UnauthorizedAccess acquisition is capped at five retries, separately from sharing contention; auth-file contention has a 30-second budget. Cancellation after successful acquisition closes the lease before returning. Only native sharing/lock codes are retried; unrelated IO errors fail immediately.",
  "regressionCharacterization": {
    "log": "artifacts/parity/current-pi-deltas-2026-10-13/auth-lock-full-tests.log",
    "sha256": "91aa8d92bf9f6649e85d74782d966411c0026963e112d554fd999532ce638d11",
    "failed": 8,
    "passed": 1559,
    "skipped": 0,
    "finding": "Seven PTY checks exposed lock creation during read-only startup; direct CLI execution confirmed read-only filesystem failure at the home credential lock. Reads/listings now avoid file mutation and new absent-directory guards cover both paths. One HTTP retry-delay check exposed a separately reproduced provider-rejection/cancellation race, fixed and recorded independently."
  },
